[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1029057455","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404#issuecomment-1029057455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404","id":1029057455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE849Viuv","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-03T14:40:55Z","updated_at":"2022-02-03T14:44:30Z","body":"_updated to note being on Fedora's list_\r\n\r\nI'm +1 to add, I think this meets the inclusion principles' factors:\r\n\r\n## Has the license been approved by the OSI?\r\n*All OSI-approved license will be included on the SPDX License List, regardless of other factors*\r\n\r\nNo\r\n\r\n## Definitive factors\r\n*These must all be satisfied to allow inclusion in the license list*\r\n\r\n### Is the submitted license unique, that is, it does not match another license already on the License List as per the matching guidelines?\r\n\r\nYes, appears to be unique\r\n\r\n### If a software license, does it apply to source code and not only to executables?\r\n\r\nNot a software license\r\n\r\n### Does the license have identifiable and stable text, and is not in the midst of drafting?\r\n\r\nYes - historical license\r\n\r\n### Has the license steward, if any, committed to versioning new versions in the future and to not modify it after addition to the list?\r\n\r\n@jlovejoy I'm assuming you aren't aware of anyone from Arphic Technology to weigh in on this? Either way, this appears to be a longstanding historical license so versioning doesn't seem a significant issue here.\r\n\r\n## Other factors for inclusion\r\n*Roughly in order of descending importance*\r\n\r\n### 1. Does the license substantially comply with one of the free/open content definitions?\r\n*Approval by the organisation that publishes the definition is not required*\r\n\r\nYes, in my view it substantially complies. It's a copyleft-style license based on bits of the GPL. [FSF describes it](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/license-list.en.html#Arphic) as a \"copyleft free software license, incompatible with the GPL.\" And @jlovejoy noted that it's on Fedora's \"good\" list.\r\n\r\nThere are a couple oddities, in particular that it requires retaining not just the license text generally but rather in a specific named file (Section 1). I'm also not sure what it means for a font to \"read[s] commands interactively when run\" (Section 2(c)). But I don't view those as changing the calculus on it being a copyleft-style license for fonts, and it looks like the FSF takes the same view that it is free.\r\n\r\n### 2. Does the license have substantial use such that it is likely to be encountered (ie. use in many projects, or in one significant project)?\r\n*For recently written licenses, definitive plans for it to be used in at least one significant project satisfies this*\r\n\r\n@jlovejoy I think you're indicating that this is used in one or more Fedora projects, is that correct? The SourceGraph link isn't showing any matches when I click on it.\r\n\r\n### 3. Is the license structured to be generally usable by anyone, and not specific to one organisation or project?\r\n\r\nNo -- specific to particular fonts owned by Arphic Technology Co.\r\n\r\n### 4. Is the license primarily intended to facilitate the free distribution of content with limited restrictions?\r\n\r\nYes\r\n\r\n### 5. Does the license steward support this submission, or is at least aware of and not in opposition of it?\r\n\r\n@jlovejoy please confirm but I think the answer is \"No\"\r\n\r\n## Summary of factors / outcome\r\n*Comments on the totality of these \"other factors\" in light of the SPDX License List's overall goals and objectives*\r\n\r\nAlthough it's specific to one company / set of files, given its conformance to the Free Software Definition and presence on FSF's and Fedora's lists, I think that the factors tilt in favor of adding it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1029057455/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1029140635","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404#issuecomment-1029140635","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404","id":1029140635,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE849V3Cb","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-03T16:01:55Z","updated_at":"2022-02-03T16:01:55Z","body":"@swinslow - I did not try to find or reach out to the license steward, so that's really an unknown. (It's also unknown if it was submitted to OSI, but we don't have that option in the drop-down)\r\n\r\nAs for the Sourcegraph link - I think some settings got messed up. Here's a revised one: https://sourcegraph.com/search?q=context:global+r:src.fedoraproject.org+file:.*%5C.spec%24+%5ELicense:%5Cs%2B.*arphic+TIMEOUT:120s&patternType=regexp\r\n- this shows the license appears in two packages that are part of the current Fedora release. (note: technically, this shows that this Fedora license id is used in the license field of the spec file for two packages in Fedora. I've been trusting this, but double checking if it's only one package)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1029140635/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1029260264","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404#issuecomment-1029260264","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404","id":1029260264,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE849WUPo","user":{"login":"silverhook","id":3227264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjcyNjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3227264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/silverhook","html_