XML/issues/comments/1035415229","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404#issuecomment-1035415229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404","id":1035415229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE849ty69","user":{"login":"seabass-labrax","id":79224200,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MjI0MjAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79224200?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax","html_url":"https://github.com/seabass-labrax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/seabass-labrax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-10T19:46:52Z","updated_at":"2022-02-10T19:46:52Z","body":"> There are a couple oddities, in particular that it requires retaining not just the license text generally but rather in a specific named file (Section 1). I'm also not sure what it means for a font to \"read[s] commands interactively when run\" (Section 2(c)). But I don't view those as changing the calculus on it being a copyleft-style license for fonts, and it looks like the FSF takes the same view that it is free.\r\n\r\n@swinslow, it certainly is a little strange, because as far as I'm aware TrueType fonts cannot read commands themselves, instead being completely under the control of the font rendering engine! I wonder if the fonts that this licence was originally written for were in a different format that allowed the fonts to read their own commands.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1035415229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1036308479","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404#issuecomment-1036308479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1404","id":1036308479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE849xM__","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-11T15:05:22Z","updated_at":"2022-02-11T15:05:22Z","body":"@seabass-labrax Interesting -- that could be! Though my guess is that it looks like they just copied this text from section 2(c) of GPL-2.0... whether or not that actually made any sense in context  :wink:","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"http